    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-2016-p7.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since any number with an even exponent is a perfect square, we can eliminate A, C, and E. Also, a square number to any power remains a square number, so that rules out D.\n\nThus, B is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Even exponents automatically make perfect squares.",
        "Also remember that a perfect-square base raised to any positive integer power stays a square."
